# "Other creatures you control get +2/+2 and gain trample": the Saga itself is not among them. To see the Saga after its
# chapter III has resolved, II and III trigger together (CR 714.2c), so that II is still on the stack and the Saga is not
# yet sacrificed (CR 714.4). On turn 9 Esper Origins is flashed back and Summon: Esper Maduin enters with one lore counter
# (Innkeeper's Talent is at level 2, so it does not double it); chapter I resolves; the Talent is raised to level 3; and
# Tezzeret's Gambit proliferates the Saga's lore counter, which the Talent doubles (CR 122.6, 701.34a): from one to three,
# II and III trigger at once.
# III resolves first: Llanowar Elves (three +1/+1 counters from the Talent's combat triggers on turns 3, 5 and 7, a 4/4)
# get +2/+2 and trample, a 6/6; the Saga stays a 4/4 without trample. Then II adds {G}{G}, and the Saga, done, is
# sacrificed and exiled for its finality counter (CR 122.1h).

